                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/1195</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Peruvian Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Prada</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-16"><hi rendition="#italic">December 16,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellent Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform Your
                    Excellency that my Government has appointed as President of the Counsel of Peru
                    in the arbitration of Tacna-Arica, Doctor Solon Polo in place of Doctor Melitón
                    F. Porras, who has resigned.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. González Prada</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
